; expect 34
; A STRUCT VARIANT declaration: `(Rect { w : Int, h : Int })`. stage1
; could not parse the braces at all, so a `data` declaration using them
; failed the whole module.
;
; A named constructor IS a positional one that also knows what its
; fields are called: arity, per-field float flags and per-field type
; nodes are built exactly as the positional spelling builds them, and
; the names ride along in a slot nothing else reads. That is why a
; POSITIONAL pattern over a named declaration - this case - needs no
; further work anywhere downstream.
;
; The named pattern spelling `(Rect { h = h, w = w })` is separate and
; is not exercised here.
(data Shape
  (Rect { w : Int, h : Int }))
(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (match (Rect 3 4)
    ((Rect w h) (+ (* w 10) h))))
